<p>I've downvoted the other 4K submissions so far, but I leave this one at a novote.</p>
<p>The whole thing is really well written, and works (I think) as a good intro to the Sloth's Pit canon of which I've read very, very little. That being said, I was definitely expecting more of a climax.</p>
<p>The Chekov's Gun here was the Goatman becoming real and the Foundation dealing with it, but that gun was never fired. It leaves space open for more, but&#8230; I feel like the &quot;more&quot; should already be here.</p>
<p>I feel quite conflicted about this piece.</p>

